@startuml how_it_flies
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  BorderColor #555555
  RoundCorner 10
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
  BorderColor #999999
}

title How the drone flies the course, start to finish

rectangle "1. BEFORE THE RACE (laptop)" as before {
  rectangle "Course map\n(organizer's published\ngate positions)" as map
  rectangle "Camera + levers\nconfig/vehicle_cam35_120.toml\n(mount angle, lens,\ntilt, slew, speed limits)" as cfg
  rectangle "Planner\nraceline.ladder --k\nsolves the fastest line\ninside the levers" as planner
  rectangle "The plan\nplan_LADDER_kNNN.json\n(the line, speed at every\npoint, 23 crossings)" as plan
  map --> planner
  cfg --> planner
  planner --> plan
}

rectangle "2. ON THE DRONE, 50 TIMES A SECOND (Orin)" as loop {
  rectangle "Flight controller\n(Betaflight over MSP)\ngives: attitude, heading,\naccel, barometer" as fc
  rectangle "Camera\n1080p 60 fps\nHSV detector finds\nred blobs" as cam
  rectangle "ESTIMATOR: where am I?\n\n- integrate accel on attitude\n  (walking with eyes closed)\n- baro + accel = altitude\n- a blob that fits the map's\n  predicted azimuth = a fix\n- passing a gate = a fix\n- counts its own crossings" as est
  rectangle "FOLLOWER: steer\n\n- where on the plan am I\n- carrot a little ahead\n- desired acceleration\n- desired altitude, nose" as fol
  rectangle "Sticks\nANGLE mode: tilt angles\n+ throttle + yaw\nover MSP" as sticks
  fc --> est
  cam --> est
  est --> fol
  plan --> fol
  fol --> sticks
  sticks --> fc
}

rectangle "3. THE HUMAN (radio)" as human {
  rectangle "Pilot arms,\nflips MSP OVERRIDE\nand ANGLE.\nCan take the sticks\nback any time." as pilot
}
pilot --> fc

note right of est
  The map is trusted. Only the gate
  just passed and the next one may
  match a blob. A blob far from the
  predicted azimuth is ignored.
end note

note bottom of fol
  Through the hairpin and the
  stacked gate the next gate is
  out of view: the follower flies
  the known turn from the plan on
  dead reckoning.
end note

@enduml
